#* {{quote-book|en|author=Basil Cottle|authorlink=Basil Cottle|title=The Penguin Dictionary of Surnames|publisher={{w|Penguin Books}}|year=1967|year_published=1969|page=109|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/penguindictionar00cott/page/109/mode/1up|passage=Fraser Recorded in Scotland in mid-1100s as ''de Frisselle'', ''de Freseliere'', ''de Fresel'', as if from a place in France, and Sir Simon F— (executed 1306) is referred to as ''Simond Frysel''; first element ?‘ash tree’ {{smallcaps|of}}, the –er ?to make it ‘'''strawberrier'''’ – a pun on the three silver cinquefoils or ''fraises'' in their armorials.}}
