#* {{quote-book|en|author=Glenn Andrews|title=Impromptu Cooking|location=New York, N.Y.|publisher=[[w:Atheneum Books|Atheneum]]|year=1973|page=216|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/impromptucooking00andr/page/216/mode/1up|isbn=0-689-10581-9|passage=And your strawberry ice cream can be the '''strawberriest''' and your peach ice cream the peachiest.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=sue ellen farmer|journal=The Student|month=fall|year=1975|page=thirty-seven|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/wakefo_thestudent7576/page/n40/mode/1up|column=2|passage=lessons exist because frozen strawberries in store are easier to pick but wild strawberries taste '''strawberrier'''.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Barbara [Halloran] Gibbons|authorlink=Barbara Halloran Gibbons|title=The International Slim Gourmet Cookbook|publisher=[[w:Harper (publisher)|Harper & Row]]|year=1978|page=324|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/internationalsli00gibb/page/324/mode/1up|isbn=0-06-011507-6|passage=My '''strawberriest''' of strawberry sauces was simply strawberries, whirred until chunky in the blender, then spooned over vanilla ice cream (or, in this case, low-fat ice milk).}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|journal={{w|Family Circle}}|date=5 June 1979|page=41|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/family-circle-magazine-1979-06-05/page/41/mode/1up|passage={{ruby|Now Jell-[O](BRAND)® Strawberry Flavor Gelatin tastes even '''Strawberrier'''.}}}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Barbara [Halloran] Gibbons|authorlink=Barbara Halloran Gibbons|title=Slim Gourmet Sweets and Treats|location=New York, N.Y.|publisher=[[w:Harper (publisher)|Harper & Row]]|year=1982|page=11|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/slimgourmetsweet00gibb/page/11/mode/1up|isbn=0-06-015057-2|passage=When used to sweeten out-of-season California strawberries, the berries are not only sweeter but “'''strawberrier''',” with a flavor more like home-grown or field-ripened fruit.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Les Fox|author2=Sue Fox|title=The Beanie Baby Handbook|publisher=West Highland Publishing Company|year=1998|page=161|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/beaniebabyhandbo00foxl_0/page/161/mode/1up|isbn=1892141-01-9|passage=Kiwi, Kiwi, chirping bright / In the forests of the night / Only a Kiwi could be merrier / About shortcake so '''strawberrier'''!}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Nigella Lawson|authorlink=Nigella Lawson|title=How to Be a Domestic Goddess: Baking and the Art of Comfort Cooking|location=London|publisher={{w|Chatto & Windus}}|year=2000|page=347|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/howtobedomesticg0000laws_i3l2/page/347/mode/1up|isbn=0 7011 6888 9|passage=It occurred to me when I was last making the strawberries in dark syrup from ''How to Eat'' that there was no reason why I couldn’t use the balsamic vinegar – which provides the darkness and really does seem to make the strawberries '''strawberrier''' – when making jam.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|journal=[[w:Sunset (magazine)|Sunset]]|month=May|year=2004|page=127|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/sunset212213maysout/page/n140/mode/1up|passage=It’s the '''strawberriest''' shortcake ever.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Rowan Clifford|title=Rodeo Ron and His Milkshake Cows|url=https://archive.org/details/rodeoronhismilks0000clif/page/n18/mode/1up|publisher=Borzoi Books|year=2005|isbn=0-375-93195-3|passage=Down leaped Ron and milked the frothiest, fruitiest, '''strawberriest''' milkshake anybody had ever tasted.}}
